From: BedrockOnLinux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] jscript: call, not get, when METHOD|PROPERTYGET carries
 arguments

disp_call() sends DISPATCH_METHOD|DISPATCH_PROPERTYGET for a call with
arguments whenever it cannot see a jsdisp yet. That is the case on the
first use of an mshtml object whose script object the call itself
creates, so in ES5+ modes the first document.createElement("div") of a
page came back as the createElement function. Knockout's IE detection
throws on that, and pages built on it, such as the Office sign-in that
Minecraft Education opens, render no form. A getter takes no arguments,
so positional arguments mean a call.
---
 dlls/jscript/dispex.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/jscript/dispex.c b/dlls/jscript/dispex.c
index dc2ff9f6a55..a032d1e2b46 100644
--- a/dlls/jscript/dispex.c
+++ b/dlls/jscript/dispex.c
@@ -2136,8 +2136,13 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI DispatchEx_InvokeEx(IWineJSDispatch *iface, DISPID id, LCI
     if(pspCaller)
         IServiceProvider_AddRef(pspCaller);
 
+    /* A getter takes no arguments, so with positional arguments the caller can
+     * only mean a call. disp_call() sends both flags for a call with arguments
+     * whenever it cannot see a jsdisp yet, which happens on the first use of an
+     * mshtml object whose script object that very call creates. */
     if(wFlags == (DISPATCH_METHOD | DISPATCH_PROPERTYGET))
-        wFlags = (This->ctx->version < SCRIPTLANGUAGEVERSION_ES5) ? DISPATCH_METHOD : DISPATCH_PROPERTYGET;
+        wFlags = (This->ctx->version < SCRIPTLANGUAGEVERSION_ES5 || (pdp && pdp->cArgs > pdp->cNamedArgs))
+            ? DISPATCH_METHOD : DISPATCH_PROPERTYGET;
 
     switch(wFlags) {
     case DISPATCH_METHOD:
